BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F2 13.5 Tf 72.00 605.00 Td (1. The problem) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 585.00 Td (Training a model means finding parameters that make a loss function small. For a parameter) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 569.00 Td (vector w and a loss L\(w\), we look for the w that minimises L. For most models there is no) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 553.00 Td (closed-form solution, so we search iteratively.) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F2 13.5 Tf 72.00 516.00 Td (2. The update rule) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 496.00 Td (The gradient of L points in the direction of steepest increase of the loss. Gradient descent) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 480.00 Td (takes a small step in the opposite direction:) Tj ET
0.906 0.886 0.863 rg 72 441.00 468 27 re f
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F3 10 Tf 80.00 451.00 Td (w\(t+1\) = w\(t\) - eta * grad L\(w\(t\)\)) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 415.00 Td (Here eta > 0 is the learning rate. Repeating this update moves w downhill until the gradient is) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 399.00 Td (close to zero.) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F2 13.5 Tf 72.00 362.00 Td (3. A one-dimensional example) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 342.00 Td (Let L\(w\) = \(w - 3\)^2, so the derivative is L'\(w\) = 2\(w - 3\) and the minimum is at w = 3. Starting) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 326.00 Td (from w = 0 with eta = 0.1:) Tj ET
0.906 0.886 0.863 rg 72 235.00 468 79 re f
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F3 10 Tf 80.00 297.00 Td (t   w\(t\)     L'\(w\(t\)\)   w\(t+1\)) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F3 10 Tf 80.00 284.00 Td (0   0.0000   -6.0000    0.6000) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F3 10 Tf 80.00 271.00 Td (1   0.6000   -4.8000    1.0800) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F3 10 Tf 80.00 258.00 Td (2   1.0800   -3.8400    1.4640) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F3 10 Tf 80.00 245.00 Td (3   1.4640   -3.0720    1.7712) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 209.00 Td (Each step closes 20% of the remaining distance to the minimum, because w\(t\) - 3 = 0.8^t * \(0) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 193.00 Td (- 3\). After 20 steps w is about 2.965.) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F2 13.5 Tf 72.00 156.00 Td (4. Choosing the learning rate) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 136.00 Td (For this loss, every update multiplies the error w - 3 by \(1 - 2 * eta\). The iteration therefore) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 120.00 Td (converges when |1 - 2 * eta| < 1, that is when 0 < eta < 1. With eta = 0.5 it reaches the) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 104.00 Td (minimum in a single step. With eta = 1 the error flips sign without shrinking, so w alternates) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 88.00 Td (between 0 and 6. With eta > 1 the error grows and the method diverges.) Tj ET
