BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F2 13.5 Tf 72.00 612.00 Td (5. Stochastic and mini-batch variants) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 592.00 Td (When the loss is an average over n training examples, computing the full gradient costs O\(n\)) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 576.00 Td (per step. Stochastic gradient descent \(SGD\) estimates the gradient from a single example,) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 560.00 Td (and mini-batch gradient descent from a small batch, typically between 32 and 512 examples.) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 544.00 Td (The estimate is noisy, but each step is far cheaper, and the noise can help the search move) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 528.00 Td (past flat regions and shallow local minima.) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F2 13.5 Tf 72.00 491.00 Td (6. Momentum) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 471.00 Td (Momentum keeps a running velocity v that accumulates past gradients:) Tj ET
0.906 0.886 0.863 rg 72 419.00 468 40 re f
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F3 10 Tf 80.00 442.00 Td (v\(t+1\) = beta * v\(t\) + grad L\(w\(t\)\)) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F3 10 Tf 80.00 429.00 Td (w\(t+1\) = w\(t\) - eta * v\(t+1\)) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 393.00 Td (A typical value is beta = 0.9. Momentum speeds up progress along directions where the) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 377.00 Td (gradient is consistent and damps oscillations across narrow valleys. Adaptive methods such) Tj ET
BT 0.137 0.196 0.188 rg /F1 11 Tf 72.00 361.00 Td (as Adam extend the same idea with a separate step size for each parameter.) Tj ET
